    "body": "fix on issue/3628-refusal-eol · PR #3636 · pinned by the `.gitattributes` rule `examples/catalog/**/refusal.txt text eol=lf` (`git ls-files --eol` gives `w/crlf` before and `w/lf` after, with `core.autocrlf=true`) · merges when reviewed\n\nTo the reporter: after the merge, an existing checkout keeps the CRLF file. To get LF, run `git rm --cached -r examples/catalog && git reset --hard`. A fresh checkout of those files also gives LF. Commit or stash your local work first, because `git reset --hard` discards it.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
